# Valgrind suppressions for ImGit's memory checks (test/CMakeLists.txt's imgit_tests.valgrind and
# tools/memcheck/run_app.sh): reports from third-party code that are not ImGit's to fix. An entry matches when the
# report's stack passes through the library it names, so memory ImGit allocates itself is never hidden; memory such
# a library hands ImGit to free would be, so keep entries to libraries whose results ImGit does not own. Generate new
# entries with `--gen-suppressions=all` and say above each which library it belongs to and why it is harmless.

# Mesa's GL driver (llvmpipe on the headless CI runner): per-process driver state it keeps until exit, and the
# llvmpipe JIT's code, which Valgrind cannot see into.
{
   mesa-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libgallium*
}
{
   mesa-dri-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/dri/*
}
{
   mesa-glx-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libGLX_mesa.so*
}
{
   llvm-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libLLVM*
}
{
   llvmpipe-jit-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   obj:*/libgallium*
}
{
   llvmpipe-jit-value
   Memcheck:Value8
   ...
   obj:*/libgallium*
}

# Xlib / XCB, fontconfig and D-Bus (through GLFW and the native file dialog): caches held for the process's life.
{
   x11-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libX11.so*
}
{
   xcb-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libxcb*.so*
}
{
   fontconfig-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libfontconfig.so*
}
{
   dbus-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   obj:*/libdbus-1.so*
}

# The dynamic loader: libraries dlopen()ed by the GL dispatch (libglvnd) stay loaded until exit.
{
   dlopen-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   fun:_dl_open
}
